The syntax of the eof() function in file handling is:

ifstream infile("filename");
while(!infile.eof())
{
    // read data from file
}

Or:

while(!infile.eof())
{
    infile >> variable;
    // process data
}

The eof() function returns true (non-zero) when the end of file is reached, and false (zero) otherwise. The NOT operator (!) is used to check if the end of file has NOT been reached, allowing the loop to continue reading until EOF is encountered.

